  "spots": [
    {
      "cell": [
        16,
        6
      ],
      "line": "A sluice board, pulled up and nailed open. The marks on the race show the water stood a yard higher here once.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        19,
        12
      ],
      "line": "Downstream the bank is gouged, and the reeds are flattened in a path the width of a cart, going up into the trees.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        22,
        7
      ],
      "line": "The store-house door is off its hinges from the inside. Grain is spilled all the way to the stream.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        17,
        9
      ],
      "line": "The ford. The stones are set for a cart's wheels, and the water runs cold over your boots."
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        6,
        14
      ],
      "line": "A wheel of the carter's, half mended, the spokes new pale wood.",
      "set_flag": "found:millrace_wheel"
    }
  ],
  "people": [
    {
      "name": "Hode the miller",
      "unit": "town_trader",
      "cell": [
        11,
        8
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "No grain, no grinding. No grinding, no bread. No bread, and I'm a man with a stopped wheel.",
        "Don't drink from below the mill. Don't ask why."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "You came by the ford? Then you saw the store-house. Don't go in. Or do. Somebody should.",
          "A mill in the woods sounded quiet. It was, for nine years."
        ],
        "again": "Back. Has the wheel turned? No. Then nothing's changed.",
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "What happened to the store-house?",
            "a": "I dammed the stream to grind for two villages. The woods flooded behind it. Something came down the race in the night and it's been in my grain since."
          },
          {
            "q": "Can the mill run again?",
            "a": "If the store-house were mine again, and somebody mended Derry's wheel, I'd have grain moving by the week's end."
          }
        ],
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "bread",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "red_draught"
          }
        ],
        "shop": "The last of the flour. I bake when I'm worried. I've been baking a lot.",
        "sold": "Mind the crust.",
        "bye": "Stay off the race."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Derry the carter",
      "unit": "peasant",
      "cell": [
        7,
        9
      ],
      "facing": [
        1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "Three wheels and an axle. I can carry anything but a fourth wheel.",
        "I'd drive the flour out myself if there were flour."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": "You've the look of people who find things. Have you seen a wheel?",
        "job": {
          "flag": "job:millrace_wheel",
          "done_flag": "found:millrace_wheel",
          "offer": "My spare wheel rolled off down the lane when the flood came. It'll be in the long grass by the meadow. Fetch it and there's coin in it.",
          "done": "That's her. New spokes and all. Here, for your trouble.",
          "gold": 900
        },
        "bye": "Watch the ruts."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Wenna, the miller's girl",
      "unit": "village_idiot",
      "cell": [
        20,
        10
      ],
      "facing": [
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "I saw it. Big as a cart and it shone wet. Father says it was a log.",
        "If you're going in the store-house, take a lamp. And a bigger friend."
      ]
    }
  ],
